---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy – Fullfill">
  <section class="privacy-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p><span class="effective-date">Updated 15 Nov 2026</span></p>

      <p>Fullfill is here to help you grow, not to hoard data or sell your information. This page explains what we collect, why, who we share it with, and how you stay in control.</p>

      <h2>1. Who Is Responsible</h2>
      <p>The controller for your data is PALITECH, Grafenberger Allee 114, 40237 D&uuml;sseldorf, Germany. Email: <a href="mailto:hello@fullfill.me">hello@fullfill.me</a></p>
      <p>This policy covers the Fullfill app, the Fullfill websites (fullfill.app, fullfill.me) and all related services.</p>

      <h2>2. What We Collect and Why</h2>

      <h3>A. Account Data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Name, email address and login details. Sign-in is handled by Firebase Authentication. We never see your password in plain text.</li>
        <li><strong>Anonymous accounts:</strong> if you skip registration, we create an anonymous account so your progress can be saved. It has no name or email, only a random ID. You can turn it into a full account later by registering.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><em>Why:</em> to create and run your account. Legal basis: performance of our contract with you (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).</p>

      <h3>B. Your Content</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Journal entries, reflections, check-ins, routines, saved activities and progress.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><em>Why:</em> to provide the app and personalise your journey. Some of this may say something about your mental wellbeing. We use it only to provide Fullfill to you, based on your consent (Art. 9(2)(a) GDPR), which you can withdraw at any time by deleting the content or your account. Your content is never used for advertising and is never shared with Meta or other ad partners.</p>

      <h3>C. Subscriptions and Payments</h3>
      <p>Payments are processed by Apple (App Store) or Google (Google Play). We never see or store your card details. We use RevenueCat to check your subscription status. It receives an app user ID, your store purchase details (product, price, dates, trial and renewal status) and basic device information. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.</p>

      <h3>D. Usage and Device Data</h3>
      <p>We use Firebase (Google) for analytics and crash reports. This includes device type, operating system, app version, language, timezone and how features are used. <em>Why:</em> to fix bugs and improve Fullfill. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in a stable, useful app (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR), or your consent where the law requires it.</p>

      <h3>E. Advertising Measurement (Meta)</h3>
      <p>We use the Meta SDK to measure and improve our ads. It sends app events, such as app installs, app opens and completed registrations, to Meta Platforms Ireland Ltd., together with device information and, where you allow it, your device's advertising ID. This tells us which ads lead people to Fullfill and helps Meta show our ads to people who may be interested.</p>
      <p>Your journal entries and other personal content are never sent to Meta. Where the law requires your consent for this, we ask for it first (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, &sect; 25 TDDDG), and you can withdraw it at any time. On iPhone, the advertising ID is only used if you allow tracking in Apple's prompt (Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security &rarr; Tracking). On Android you can reset or delete it in Settings &rarr; Google &rarr; Ads.</p>

      <h3>F. Notifications</h3>
      <p>If you allow notifications, we use OneSignal to send reminders, including a reminder before a free trial ends. OneSignal stores a push token, basic device information, your timezone and your notification settings. You can turn notifications off at any time in your device settings. Legal basis: your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).</p>

      <h3>G. AI Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>We use secure third-party AI services for features such as transcription and personalisation. Only the data needed for the feature is sent.</li>
        <li>Your entries are not used to train public AI models.</li>
        <li>AI outputs are stored only as long as needed.</li>
        <li>You can opt out of AI features at any time.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>H. Our Websites</h3>
      <p>Our websites are hosted by Vercel and Netlify. Like any web server, they process your IP address and basic browser information in short-term logs to deliver pages and keep the sites secure (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>

      <h2>3. Who We Share Data With</h2>
      <p>We never sell your data. We share it only with service providers who help run Fullfill and who process it on our behalf or under their own terms where stated:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Firebase</strong>: sign-in (including anonymous accounts), database and analytics</li>
        <li><strong>RevenueCat</strong>: subscription status</li>
        <li><strong>Apple and Google</strong>: payments and subscriptions through their app stores</li>
        <li><strong>OneSignal</strong>: push notifications</li>
        <li><strong>Meta</strong>: ad measurement and attribution, as described above</li>
        <li><strong>AI service providers</strong>: for AI features you use</li>
        <li><strong>Vercel and Netlify</strong>: website hosting</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Some of these providers process data in the United States. Where that happens, transfers are protected by the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or by the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>

      <h2>4. How Long We Keep Your Data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Account data and your content, including anonymous accounts: for as long as your account exists. When you delete your account, they are deleted.</li>
        <li>Technical logs kept for security and fraud prevention: up to 30 days.</li>
        <li>Analytics data: kept in pseudonymous form for a limited period set in our analytics settings, then deleted.</li>
        <li>Records we must keep by law, for example for tax purposes: for the period the law requires.</li>
        <li>Apple, Google and Meta keep data under their own retention policies.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Deleting Your Account</h2>
      <p>In the app, go to Settings &rarr; Account &rarr; Delete Account. Deletion is immediate and permanent. This also works for anonymous accounts. Because an anonymous account has no email address, please delete it from inside the app.</p>
      <p>If you can't access the app, see <a href="/delete">how to request deletion</a> or email <a href="mailto:hello@fullfill.me">hello@fullfill.me</a> from the address you signed up with. Email requests are processed within 7 days.</p>
      <p>Deleting the app or your account does not cancel a subscription. Cancel it in the App Store or Google Play.</p>

      <h2>6. Your Rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Access the data we hold about you</li>
        <li>Correct mistakes</li>
        <li>Delete your data or export it</li>
        <li>Restrict or object to processing, including processing based on legitimate interest</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent at any time, without affecting processing that happened before</li>
        <li>Complain to a data protection authority. Ours is the Landesbeauftragte f&uuml;r Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit Nordrhein-Westfalen (<a href="https://www.ldi.nrw.de" rel="noopener">ldi.nrw.de</a>)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@fullfill.me">hello@fullfill.me</a> to use any of these rights.</p>

      <h2>7. How We Protect Your Data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>HTTPS encryption</li>
        <li>Secure cloud storage</li>
        <li>Strict access control</li>
        <li>Regular security checks</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Age</h2>
      <p>Fullfill is for adults aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect data from children.</p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy when Fullfill changes. The date at the top shows the latest version. If a change is significant, we will tell you in the app or by email.</p>

      <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>Questions or privacy concerns? Email <a href="mailto:hello@fullfill.me">hello@fullfill.me</a>. We read every message.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-section {
    font-family: var(--font-urbanist);
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 60px 20px;
  }

  .container {
    width: 100%;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin-top: 30px;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 1.1em;
    margin-top: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .effective-date {
    color: var(--text-secondary, #666);
  }

  ul {
    margin-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  em {
    font-style: italic;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .privacy-section {
      padding: 40px 20px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 1.8rem;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    p {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
  }
</style>

<style>
  .privacy-section { color: var(--color-text-body); }
  .privacy-section h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-urbanist);
    font-size: var(--type-hero) !important;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--color-dark-purple);
  }
  .privacy-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-urbanist);
    font-size: var(--type-card) !important;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-brand);
  }
  .privacy-section h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-urbanist);
    font-size: 20px !important;
    color: var(--color-dark-purple);
  }
  .privacy-section p,
  .privacy-section li { font-size: var(--type-body) !important; line-height: 1.5; }
  .privacy-section a { color: var(--color-brand); }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .privacy-section h1 { font-size: var(--type-section) !important; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 575px) {
    .privacy-section h1 { font-size: var(--type-section) !important; }
  }
</style>
